        "file": "dora.py",
        "lang": "python",
        "kind": "neutral",
        "code": "from datetime import datetime\n\n# One tuple per production deployment over the last 7 days:\n# (commit time, deploy time, caused an incident?, minutes to restore)\ndeployments = [\n    (\"2026-03-02 09:10\", \"2026-03-02 11:40\", False, 0),\n    (\"2026-03-02 14:05\", \"2026-03-03 10:15\", False, 0),\n    (\"2026-03-04 08:30\", \"2026-03-04 09:00\", True, 45),\n    (\"2026-03-05 16:20\", \"2026-03-06 09:50\", False, 0),\n    (\"2026-03-06 10:00\", \"2026-03-06 15:30\", True, 15),\n]\nDAYS = 7\nFORMAT = \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M\"\n\n# Lead time: hours between the commit and its arrival in production\nlead_times = []\nfor commit, deploy, _, _ in deployments:\n    delta = datetime.strptime(deploy, FORMAT) - datetime.strptime(commit, FORMAT)\n    lead_times.append(delta.total_seconds() / 3600)\n\nfailures = [d for d in deployments if d[2]]\n\nprint(f\"Deployment frequency  : {len(deployments) / DAYS:.2f} per day\")\nprint(f\"Lead time for changes : {sum(lead_times) / len(lead_times):.1f} hours on average\")\nprint(f\"Change failure rate   : {100 * len(failures) / len(deployments):.0f} %\")\nprint(f\"Time to restore       : {sum(d[3] for d in failures) / len(failures):.0f} minutes on average\")\n",
        "output": "Deployment frequency  : 0.71 per day\nLead time for changes : 9.2 hours on average\nChange failure rate   : 40 %\nTime to restore       : 30 minutes on average\n",
        "note": {
          "fr": "Quatre chiffres suffisent à décrire la livraison d'une équipe. Ici elle livre presque chaque jour et répare vite, mais 2 déploiements sur 5 provoquent un incident : c'est le point à améliorer, par exemple avec plus de tests automatiques.",
          "en": "Four numbers are enough to describe a team's delivery. Here it ships almost every day and repairs fast, but 2 deployments out of 5 cause an incident: that is the point to improve, for example with more automated tests."
        }
